  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## TF-IDF + Logistic Regression Pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "Building the full pipeline as a single sklearn `Pipeline` object. This is critical — it ensures TF-IDF is **fit only on training data**. Fitting on the full dataset and then splitting would leak term frequencies from test articles into the feature matrix.\n",
    "\n",
    "**TF-IDF settings:**\n",
    "- `max_features=50000` — vocabulary capped at top 50k tokens by corpus frequency\n",
    "- `ngram_range=(1,2)` — unigrams and bigrams; bigrams capture phrases like \"breaking news\" or \"unnamed sources\"\n",
    "\n",
    "**Logistic Regression:**\n",
    "- `class_weight='balanced'` — weights inversely proportional to class frequency, compensating for the fake/real imbalance"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 18,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "pipeline = Pipeline([\n",
    "    (\"tfidf\", TfidfVectorizer()),\n",
    "    (\"lr\", LogisticRegression())\n",
    "])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
